cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, its methodology, or results obtained with it,
  please cite this software release and the relevant methodological
  publications listed below.

title: SISO Adaptive Control
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-29

author:
  - family-names: Bukovsky
    given-names: Ivo

repository-code: https://github.com/simple-machine-learning/SISO-Adaptive-Control
url: https://github.com/simple-machine-learning/SISO-Adaptive-Control

abstract: >-
  A unified research and teaching environment for data-driven identification
  and control of simulated and measured SISO systems. The software supports
  LNU- and QNU-based plant identification and model-reference adaptive control,
  as well as conventional model predictive control using LNU, QNU, or MLP
  predictive plant models. It includes one-step and recursive multi-step
  prediction, frozen-model and sliding-retraining MPC, spectral-radius
  diagnostics for learned recursive-model loop stability, BIBS-oriented
  monitoring, and 38 physical ODE plant models in the simulated workflow.
  Version 1.0.0 is distributed as a portable pure-Python edition and a Linux
  edition with selected native performance improvements.

keywords:
  - small data machine learning
  - data-driven control
  - system identification
  - SISO systems
  - higher-order neural units
  - HONU
  - LNU
  - QNU
  - MLP
  - model reference adaptive control
  - MRAC
  - model predictive control
  - MPC
  - spectral radius
  - BIBS stability

